*.iml
.gradle/
# Gradle's own Kotlin-compiler-daemon/session working directory at the repo root — same root cause as the
# build/ rule below (only ever appears once a real local Kotlin/JVM build runs, e.g. `gradle :desktop:build`).
.kotlin/

# Python bytecode from the tools/ scripts. Same class of gap as the leading-slash `build/` fixed
# earlier: harmless while nothing here ever ran locally, real now that it does.
#
# ⚠️ These two lines were inserted INTO the middle of the two-line comment above, which left `# build/`
# commented out on its own and appended the sentence's tail to the `*.pyc` line — so git read the whole
# of `*.pyc rule below (only ever appears …)` as ONE pattern, which matches nothing. `*.pyc` has not
# been ignored since. Nothing showed it, because every .pyc CPython writes lands inside a
# `__pycache__/` directory that the line above already covers; a stray one written anywhere else was
# committable. Keep a rule and its comment adjacent, and never split a wrapped comment to insert.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/local.properties
/.idea/
.DS_Store
# No leading slash — matches every module's build/ dir (app/build/, core/telemetry/build/,
# desktop/build/, …), not just one at the repo root. Never actually bit anything before this
# session because every prior build ran on an ephemeral CI runner; now that a local Kotlin/JVM
# build (:desktop) genuinely runs here too, an unscoped rule is the correct fix, not a one-off.
build/
/captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# The acoustic interrogator's native upstreams. CI shallow-clones whisper.cpp and llama.cpp at a
# pinned tag into app/src/main/cpp/ before Gradle runs — they are never vendored, because a git
# submodule needs a pinned commit SHA and the development container cannot reach GitHub to obtain
# one. Listed BEFORE those clone steps exist, deliberately: `git add -A` has already swept one
# stray file into a commit this session, and a multi-megabyte C++ tree is the same mistake with a
# much worse blast radius.
app/src/main/cpp/whisper.cpp/
app/src/main/cpp/llama.cpp/
# quickjs-ng, on the same terms and for the same reason — it is the JavaScript engine yt-dlp needs
# for YouTube, cloned at a pinned tag by the same workflow.
app/src/main/cpp/quickjs/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
local.defaults.properties

# The debug keystore is intentionally committed so every CI build is signed with the
# same key — this lets the published debug APK install as an in-place UPDATE (keeping the
# user's settings + downloaded model) instead of forcing an uninstall. Debug keys are not
# secret (well-known password "android"); this is safe to commit.
!/app/debug.keystore
tools/kb/.next_wave.json

# JPL/Skyfield ephemeris kernels. These are ~17 MB binaries fetched on demand purely to generate
# expected values when validating the astronomy cores locally — the app never reads them, so they
# must not end up in the repo (or the APK).
*.bsp

# Local verification scratch: the harness is tracked, its build output and
# regenerable inputs are not (index.tsv is derived from guide_index.json).
# ⚠️ Matched by ARTIFACT TYPE, not directory name — an earlier rule named the output
# directory (scratchpad/**/out/) and a second script wrote to coreout/ instead, so 540
# .class files were committed before anyone noticed.
scratchpad/**/*.class
scratchpad/**/*.kotlin_module
scratchpad/**/*.jar
scratchpad/kb/index.tsv

# Scratch copies of tools, which have to live beside the real ones because several resolve the
# repo root from their own __file__. `git add -A` swept a 1300-line temp copy of the image sourcer
# into a commit once; a name pattern is cheaper than remembering.
tools/**/_*_TEMP.py

# Regenerable local verification input: the fallacy sweep extracts this from the bundled guide
# shards with tools-side Python. The harness is tracked; what it derives is not.
scratchpad/fallacy/prose.txt

# Measurement corpora pulled from live APIs for local validation — large, regenerable, and not
# content the app ships. The harnesses that read them ARE committed; the data they read is not.
scratchpad/**/sb_*.json
scratchpad/**/corpus.tsv

# The offline food database: ~4.5M retail barcodes, 296 MB. Built by CI (or locally with
# tools/food/build_food_db.py) and cached between runs — never committed, because GitHub hard-
# rejects files over 100 MB and this repository has no LFS. The generic-food seed.tsv IS
# committed, and lives in :core:health, whose assets both applications inherit.
app/src/main/assets/food/food.db
app/src/main/assets/food/food.db.gz
# The standalone nutrition app packages its own copy of the same database, from the same cache.
nutrition/src/main/assets/food/food.db
nutrition/src/main/assets/food/food.db.gz

# The packed Gaia star catalogue: 36.9M stars at G<15, about 295 MB. Built by CI (or locally with
# tools/sky/build_catalogue.py) and cached between runs, for the same reason as the food database
# above — GitHub hard-rejects files over 100 MB and this repository has no LFS.
#
# ⚠️ It was tracked until the deep tier landed, at 24.7 MB. Untracking it does NOT shrink `.git`:
# the old blob stays in history for ever and only future growth is avoided. Said plainly rather
# than implying a saving that is not there.
#
# ⚠️ The BRIGHT catalogue beside it — `stars.tsv`, 8,404 naked-eye stars — IS committed and must
# stay so. Gaia saturates above about G = 3 and holds none of the fifteen brightest stars in the
# sky, so the two files are the faint and bright halves of one picture rather than two versions
# of the same thing.
core/sky/src/main/assets/sky/stars.skycat
